<title>HONG KONG: IDBI sets US$150 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>IDBI sets US$150 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was</p>
<p>announced by lead manager and bookrunner Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>International.</p>
<p>BORROWER INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT BANK OF INDIA</p>
<p> AMT	US$150 MLN COUPON     6ML+60*     MATURITY    7 YRS</p>
<p> TYPE     FRN	  ISS PRICE  99.460	RE-OFFER    99.460</p>
<p> PUTS     **	   CALLS	NONE	  PAY DATE   24.APR.97</p>
<p> LISTING  LUXEMBOURG REPAYMENT  BULLET	DENOMS	US$10K</p>
<p>RATINGS  BAA3/BB+***SALES LIMITS UK/HK/S'PORE/INDIA/US NOT 144A</p>
<p> NEG PLG  YES	  CRS DEF    YES	   FORCE MAJ   IPMA2</p>
<p> GOV LAW  ENGLISH    HOME CTRY  INDIA	 TAX PROV    ---</p>
<p> FEES     50 BP AS   MGT,UND    20 BP	 SELLING     30 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    *FIXED RE-OFFER YIELD OF LIBOR +70 BP</p>
<p>	    **CAN BE PUT IF INDIA HOLDS LESS THAN 51 PCT OF</p>
<p>	    BORROWER</p>
<p>	    ***BB+ WITH POSITIVE OUTLOOK FROM S&amp;P</p>
<p> LEADS    MERRILL LYNCH INTERNATIONAL (BOOKS), ABN AMRO HOARE</p>
<p>	    GOVETT, BA ASIA, SBC WARBURG</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
